{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y+3z=-1-x \\\\ 4y=-5z \\\\ x+6z-3=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-10074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z=-1 \\\\ 4y+5z=0 \\\\ x+6z=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(24)-2(-5)+3(0-4) \\\\  & =24+10-12 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}24 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 12 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}24 & 5 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}-30 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{15}{11} \\\\ -\\frac{10}{11} \\\\ \\frac{8}{11}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-10074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "521dbf399261aa539af449884a786ee73350a9b93f5f1f04cd961fa1322612ad"} {"question" "q-10074" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-10074" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-15,y=-10,z=8"] ["math" "x=-30,y=-20,z=16"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}"] ["math" "x=15,y=10,z=8"] ["math" "x=\\frac{15}{11},y=\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-10074" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-78568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a matrix equation $A{B}^{-1}\\,x=d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $5\\times 5$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $5\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-78568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $A$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${A}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $A{B}^{-1}\\,x=d$ by ${A}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{B}^{-1}\\,x & =d \\\\ {A}^{-1}A{B}^{-1}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{5}{B}^{-1}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${B}^{-1}\\,x={A}^{-1}\\,d$ by $B,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ B{B}^{-1}\\,x & =B{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{5}\\,x & =B{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & =B{A}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-78568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "521dbf399261aa539af449884a786ee73350a9b93f5f1f04cd961fa1322612ad"} {"question" "q-78568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-78568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=BA\\,d"] ["math" "x=B\\,d\\,A"] ["math" "x=B{A}^{-1}\\,d"] ["math" "x={A}^{-1}B\\,d"] ["math" "x={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-78568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=B{A}^{-1}\\,d"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-78572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a matrix equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $5\\times 5$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $5\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-78572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d$ by $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ A{A}^{-1}\\,x & =A{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{5}\\,x & =A{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & =A{B}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-78572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "521dbf399261aa539af449884a786ee73350a9b93f5f1f04cd961fa1322612ad"} {"question" "q-78572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-78572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=A{B}^{-1}\\,d"] ["math" "x={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d"] ["math" "x={B}^{-1}A\\,d"] ["math" "x={B}^{-1}\\,d\\,A"] ["math" "x={B}^{-1}\\,d\\,{A}^{-1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-78572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=A{B}^{-1}\\,d"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-104536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+z=1 \\\\ 2x-2z=2+2y \\\\ 2y+4z=2x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-104536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+z=1 \\\\ 2x-2y-2z=2 \\\\ -2x+2y+4z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-(8-4)+(4-4) \\\\  & =-4+0 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-4}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=2+1+0=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-104536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "521dbf399261aa539af449884a786ee73350a9b93f5f1f04cd961fa1322612ad"} {"question" "q-104536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-104536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-104536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-104541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y+z+x=2 \\\\ -3z+y=3 \\\\ 2x+y=4-4z\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-104541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=2 \\\\ y-3z=3 \\\\ 2x+y+4z=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4+3)-(0+6)+(0-2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1\\text{ }\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=11,y=-6,z=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-104541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "521dbf399261aa539af449884a786ee73350a9b93f5f1f04cd961fa1322612ad"} {"question" "q-104541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-104541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-11,y=6,z=-3"] ["math" "x=11,y=-6,z=-3"] ["math" "x=11,y=6,z=3"] ["math" "x=3,y=-11,z=-6"] ["math" "x=6,y=-3,z=-11"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"} {"question" "q-104541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=11,y=-6,z=-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006196/state.json" "file_sha256" "4fb395fc63df45a11b0fc877c80fdc0980a300d5c58b0d66f000ebe59e3915d8"}] "usage" {"q-78572" []} "basis" 1113 "retractions" [[17592186092765 :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation $A^{-1}x = B^{-1}d$, where $A$ and $B$ are $5 \\cdot 5$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $5 \\cdot 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186091056 17592186091057 17592186091058 17592186091059 17592186091060] "immutable_fields" [[17592186091055 :answer-field/correct] [17592186091055 :answer-field/id] [17592186091055 :answer-field/key] [17592186091055 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
